{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler orchestrator) is requesting implementation of srd068 R2.1-R2.4 for `cmd/csplit`. This is a stitch task (task #5450) in a code generation pipeline. The specific requirements are:\n   - R2.1: `{N}` appended to a pattern must repeat that pattern N additional times (total N+1 applications)\n   - R2.2: `{*}` appended to a pattern must repeat that pattern as many times as possible until end of input\n   - R2.3: `/REGEXP/+N` and `/REGEXP/-N` must split N lines after or before the matching line\n   - R2.4: When a pattern does not match, must print an error to stderr (basic error behavior)\n\n   Acceptance criteria: `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test` must all pass. Differential tests against `gcsplit` must pass.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU csplit utility reimplementation in Go\n   - Differential testing against Homebrew reference binary (`gcsplit`)\n   - Pattern-based file splitting with regex, skip, and integer patterns\n   - Repeat counts (`{N}` and `{*}`) for pattern repetition\n   - Line offsets (`+N`/`-N`) for regex patterns\n   - pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests harness for comparing Go binary vs reference binary\n   - SIGPIPE handler required for all cmd/ utilities\n   - Files are removed on error (GNU behavior)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd068-csplit.yaml`\n     - Contains full SRD with R1-R4 requirements and acceptance criteria\n     - Key for this task: R2.1 ({N} repeat), R2.2 ({*} repeat), R2.3 (offset +N/-N), R2.4 (error on no match)\n     - non_goals: no --suppress-matched beyond basic, no --keep-files on error\n   \n   - `cmd/csplit/main.go` (existing, needs modification)\n     - Current implementation handles R1.1-R1.4 (basic pattern splitting)\n     - Key structures:\n       ```go\n       type patternKind int\n       const (\n           kindRegexp patternKind = iota\n           kindSkip\n           kindInteger\n       )\n       type pattern struct {\n           kind    patternKind\n           regex   *regexp.Regexp\n           lineNum int\n           raw     string\n       }\n       type splitter struct {\n           lines   []string\n           pos     int\n           fileNum int\n           prefix  string\n           digits  int\n           created []string\n       }\n       ```\n     - `parseDelimited()` extracts content between delimiters (requires delimiter as last char - needs modification for offsets)\n     - `parsePattern()` handles /REGEXP/, %REGEXP%, and INTEGER - needs extension for {N}/{*} and +N/-N\n     - `process()` iterates patterns sequentially - needs repeat logic\n     - `apply()` dispatches by kind - needs offset support\n     - `matchRegexp()` searches from start position - used for regex matching\n     - `emitPiece()` writes output file and prints byte count\n     - `removeFiles()` cleans up on error\n\n   - `cmd/csplit/csplit_test.go` (existing, needs modification)\n     - Uses `testutils.BuildBinary` and `exec.LookPath(\"gcsplit\")` with skip\n     - Has `normalizeErr` function to normalize binary names in error messages\n     - Existing test groups: `regexpSplitTests()`, `lineNumberTests()`, `skipPatternTests()`, `fileInputTests()`, `errorTests()`\n     - Uses `seqBytes(from, to)` helper for generating sequential number input\n     - Need to add test groups for: repeat counts ({N}, {*}), offsets (+N/-N), and error cases for R2.4\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - was interrupted before implementation began.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that the existing `parseDelimited()` function won't work for patterns with offsets (e.g., `/regex/+5`) because it requires the delimiter to be the last character\n   - The `pattern` struct needs new fields: `offset int` and `repeat int` (with -1 for `{*}`)\n   - `parsePattern()` needs to handle extraction of `{N}` and `{*}` suffixes from args before delegating to kind-specific parsing\n   - `parseDelimited()` or a new function needs to handle `/REGEXP/+N` and `/REGEXP/-N` syntax\n   - `process()` needs loop logic for repeat counts\n   - `apply()` needs to adjust the split boundary by the offset value\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The single user message is the complete task specification including: role definition, repository files list, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement_states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, shared protocols, package contracts, and constraints.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Modify `cmd/csplit/main.go` to add R2.1-R2.4 functionality:\n     - Add `offset` and `repeat` fields to `pattern` struct\n     - Modify pattern parsing to extract `{N}`, `{*}`, `+N`, `-N`\n     - Add repeat logic in `process()`\n     - Add offset adjustment in `apply()` for regex patterns\n   - Modify `cmd/csplit/csplit_test.go` to add differential tests for:\n     - `{N}` repeat counts\n     - `{*}` repeat-until-end\n     - `+N` and `-N` offsets\n     - Error cases for no match (R2.4)\n   - Verify: `go build -o bin/csplit ./cmd/csplit/` succeeds\n   - Verify: `go vet ./cmd/csplit/...` reports no issues\n   - Verify: `go test ./cmd/csplit/... -count=1` passes\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (SRD, main.go, test file) and was about to begin implementation. I had analyzed the existing code structure and identified what modifications are needed. No code has been written yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the modified `cmd/csplit/main.go` with R2.1-R2.4 support (repeat counts, offsets, error behavior), then write the modified `cmd/csplit/csplit_test.go` with new differential test cases, then run build and test verification. The task description states: \"Implement srd068 R2.1 per the SRD specification\", \"Implement srd068 R2.2 per the SRD specification\", \"Implement srd068 R2.3 per the SRD specification\", \"Implement srd068 R2.4 per the SRD specification\" with design decision \"Extend the existing csplit implementation -- do not restructure code from R1\".\n\n   Specific implementation plan:\n   1. Extend `pattern` struct with `offset int` and `repeat int` fields (0 = no repeat, -1 = {*})\n   2. Modify `parsePattern()` to strip `{N}` or `{*}` suffix before kind dispatch\n   3. Modify regex/skip parsing to handle `+N`/`-N` offset after closing delimiter\n   4. Add repeat logic in `process()` that loops pattern application\n   5. Adjust `apply()` to add offset to the match position for regex patterns\n   6. Add test functions for repeat and offset cases\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5450/f8cc86ec-d5d0-48bb-b1ea-93b487356535.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8cc86ec-d5d0-48bb-b1ea-93b487356535","uuid":"309238ff-889f-42f7-aa3c-22f7a60290c6","timestamp":"2026-05-21T20:03:41.809Z","isSynthetic":true}
