{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RQiE2iTJpbEJfe8UgxBQca","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So for the regex repeat failure:\n- First application matches: emit xx00 with \"a\\n\" (2 bytes)\n- Repeat 1 tries but no more matches: emit the rest \"x\\nb\\nc\\n\" (6 bytes), then error \"match not found on repetition 1\"\n- Exit 1 and remove files\n\nThe error format is: `csplit: '/x/': match not found on repetition 1`\n\nNow for my implementation, the process flow for `{N}` repeats with `N=2`:\n\n\n- i=0 is the first application, i=1 is the first repetition, i=2 is the second repetition, so the error correctly references \"repetition 1\" for i=1.\n\nFor integer repeats, I need to handle relative advancing differently—instead of always using `pat.lineNum - 1` as the target, I should compute it as `s.pos + pat.lineNum` when we're in a repeat iteration. I'll add a `repeated` parameter to the `apply` function to distinguish between the initial application and subsequent repetitions.\n\nActually, it might be cleaner to handle this logic directly in the `process` method by calling a separate method for integer repeats.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2663,"cache_read_input_tokens":40945,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2663},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8cc86ec-d5d0-48bb-b1ea-93b487356535","uuid":"90e87bc2-400c-49a4-bf08-557e8187365c"}
